{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the earth was corrupted.</b> The meaning is: the people of the earth. Similarly, \"when a land sins against me\" (Ezekiel 14:13); \"and all the earth came\" (Genesis 41:57)." "Some say the meaning of \"before Elohim\" is: in public. Others said that the meaning is: they were corrupted in secret and in hidden things that none but HaShem knew. What is close to me is that the Torah spoke in the language of human beings, along the path that the listeners would understand — like a servant who commits a transgression before his master and does not fear him. And those who say that Elohim in this place is not holy have said nothing at all." "<b>Violence.</b> Robbery and oppression, and also taking women by force."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {1 "'על דרד' appears to be a corruption or non-standard spelling; translated hyper-literally as 'along the path.' The phrase 'איננו קדש' is taken to mean 'is not holy' (i.e., not a divine epithet here)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:31.387789012Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}